  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1132 AM MST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nThere is decent agreement among the model guidance, with the\nexception of the GFS. It tries to bring a shortwave trough\nacross Colorado mid week, while the ECMWF, Canadian and ensemble\nguidance keep the system glancing by to the north and east.\n\nMonday through Friday...for the most part, upper level high\npressure will dominate the region through the work week. This\nwill lead to dry conditions throughout the period. Temperatures\nwill remain mild, with 50s and 60s across the Plains. The\nwarmest conditions are forecast for Monday with a few low 70s\npossible. As mentioned above, a glancing shortwave trough will\npass to the north and east sending a weak cold front across the\nPlains for mid week. This will cool high temperatures slightly\non Wednesday, before warming back Thursday into Friday.\nOvernight lows will continue to fall into the 30s across the\nPlains, and 20s for the San Luis Valley.  \n\nJust a note about the GFS being an outlier. It would bring\nisolated showers ot the Central Mountains mid week, and cooler\ntemperatures to the Plains behind a stronger cold front.",
